    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d683-a1">

                <pb facs="0834" n="740" xml:id="pg740"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 118.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Captain-General Valeriano Weyler to Mr.
                    Lee.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Army of the Island of Cuba,<lb/>Office of the Captain-General,
                                Chief of Staff</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1896-09-05"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 5,
                    1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In continuation of my official note of the
                    14th August last, I have the honor to state that, as I am informed by the
                    general governor of the Cabaña fortress, the American citizens that belonged to
                    the schooner <hi rendition="#italic">Competitor</hi> occupy the casemates
                    (calabozos) Nos. 41 and 42 of said fortress, which are the ones that are best
                    conditioned among those in the fort.</p>
                <p>God guard you many years.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Valeriano Weyler.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
